          "id": "HIMANTOPUS_HIMANTOPUS",
          "name": "Himantopus himantopus",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "Black-winged stilt",
          "lineage": "Stilts",
          "continents": [
            "Europe",
            "Asia",
            "Africa",
            "Australia"
          ],
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "The black-winged stilt is a widely distributed, very long-legged wader in the avocet and stilt family Recurvirostridae. Its scientific name, Himantopus himantopus, is sometimes used to generalize a single, almost cosmopolitan species. Alternatively, it is restricted to the form that is widespread in Europe, Asia and Africa, which equals the nominate group of H.",
          "sourcedFrom": "wikipedia",
          "children": [],
